cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline, its DFM gate, or its published measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "pcb-auto: an unattended natural-language-to-PCB pipeline with an independent DFM gate"
abstract: >-
  pcb-auto compiles a single Chinese natural-language board idea into fabrication-ready PCB
  artifacts (Gerber, Excellon drill, BOM, pick-and-place) with no human intervention, by driving
  the 嘉立创 EDA (LCEDA) CLI. Its contribution is measurement discipline rather than a demo: a
  standalone offline DFM gate that independently decides orderability, four acceptance layers, and
  a published corpus whose every figure carries its denominator, its settle window, and its as-of
  time. At the citation date the corpus held 56 settled product directories: 53 orderable, 3
  blocked; 42 of 44 board names produced at least one orderable directory; and the self-reported
  pass flag disagreed with the independent gate in the dangerous direction zero times but in the
  pessimistic direction five times. No board from this corpus has been physically manufactured.
